title the face earns its claim -- 1128 lit pixels, content-addressed, lawful in both languages; the tri-OS door booked for Dream
prompt kg on the recommended best path with gates approved: the face joins the surface-claims family, and the wayland parity run is booked where Dream's claim-as-override reads.
think The mechanism: pond/apps/lantern_face_claim.rye composes the settled reference exchange (the nine-nodes question and its answer, byte-stable on purpose), dresses it from the base sheet, rasterizes at scale one to 320x128 pixels on the house ground, and pins the two facts a backend answers for a buffer -- lit and the SHA3-256 of the visible bytes -- discover-then-pin exactly as surface_reference taught: the discovery run printed lit=1128 and the digest, the pins seated, and the green run answers them. Four legs: the pinned claim, the claims law held locally (lit inside the area), byte determinism across two compositions, and the unknown face carrying its own distinct claim -- content-addressing proven by difference. Then the night closes its own circle: tools/l/lantern_face_claim_witness.rish feeds the very pins to the mul desk src/gate/gate-surface-lit-area-u32.glow on metal -- 1128 320 128 answers 1 -- so the face's claim is proven lawful by the claims law in Glow as well as in Rye, through the rune the language grew yesterday for exactly this law. Anchors on the lit pin and claims_for.
obs The tri-OS door is BOOKED on the card for Dream's claim-as-override: the LOCA parity via brushstroke/wayland_seed.rye on the pier, pins in surface_reference.rye. No wayland witness existed in tools -- the booking names the seed and the pins, and Dream's lap shapes the run. Card bytes paid from my own lines, 24,565 of 24,576.
